.nh
.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-webhook-endpoints-update - Update a webhook endpoint


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago webhook-endpoints update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint is used to update an existing webhook endpoint. The response includes the endpoint's \fBsigning_keys\fR when the API key has write access to webhook endpoints.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--event-types\fP=""
	The list of event types sent to this webhook endpoint. Pass 'null' or '["*"]' to receive every event type. An empty array stops every delivery. Values are trimmed, lowercased and deduplicated, and an unsupported event type is rejected.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	The name of the webhook endpoint.

.PP
\fB--signature-algo\fP=""
	The algorithm used to sign the webhook payload. When the field is omitted, the current value is kept. 'null' is refused.
\&'standard_webhooks' is available to every organization. An unknown value returns a '422' error with 'value_is_invalid' on 'signature_algo'.
Switching to 'standard_webhooks' creates the endpoint's signing key, or reuses the key it kept from an earlier switch.; one of: jwt, hmac, standard_webhooks

.PP
\fB--webhook-url\fP=""
	The URL of the webhook endpoint. It must be an HTTP or HTTPS URL with a host, and it must be unique within the organization.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Allow insecure HTTP or TLS for self-hosted Lago

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Environment mode: live or test

.PP
\fB--no-retry\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic retries

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, or yaml

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Named profile to use

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath expression applied to the response

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Total request timeout

.PP
\fB--timing\fP[=false]
	Print request latency breakdown

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Print redacted request and response details


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lago webhook-endpoints update <lago_id> --input @payload.json
  lago webhook-endpoints update <lago_id> --input @payload.json --output json  # full resource
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlago-webhook-endpoints(1)\fP
